# Backend & Database Guidelines

## NestJS Architecture
- Use modular structure (Controller -> Service -> Repository / Queue).
- Validate all incoming REST requests and webhooks using Zod DTO schemas.
- Exceptions: Catch all unhandled errors using NestJS Exception Filters. Never expose raw database stack traces.

## Resiliency & Concurrency
- Downstream Rate Limiting: Mock services enforce a limit of 60 req/min. Implement BullMQ queueing with exponential backoff and jitter.
- Idempotency: All incoming access webhooks must check `request_id` against an `idempotency_keys` Postgres table before execution.
- Audit Trail: Store state transitions in an append-only `access_audit_logs` table.
